---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/help.rs
expression: shown
---
Work with Holst boards from the command line.

USAGE
  holst <command> <subcommand> [flags]

CORE COMMANDS
  board:       Work with boards and folders (alias: b)
  object:      Work with the objects on a board (alias: o)
  search:      Find boards by name and text on boards
  workspace:   Work with workspaces (alias: ws)

MORE COMMANDS
  auth:        Log in, log out and check the saved login
  backup:      List, download and restore board backups
  comment:     Read and write comment threads
  template:    Work with board templates (alias: tpl)

LOCAL COMMANDS
  storage:     See and clean what holst keeps on this machine

FLAGS
  -o, --output format   Output format: text, json or pretty; text by default
  -v, --verbose         Print request logs on stderr
      --base-url url    The Holst server; https://app.holst.so by default
      --home dir        Keep the saved login in this directory, not in the keychain
      --no-cache        Read boards from the server, not from the board cache
  -V, --version         Show the version
  -h, --help            Show help for a command

EXAMPLES
  $ holst auth login
  $ holst b ls -w easy
  $ holst b snap "Roadmap" --frame "Q3"
  $ holst o add sticker "Roadmap" "Ask design" -c yellow4
  $ holst search "retro"

LEARN MORE
  Use `holst <command> <subcommand> -h` for more information about a command.
  Learn about exit codes using `holst help exit-codes`.
  On a terminal holst asks before a held change or on several matches; `HOLST_NO_PROMPT=1` turns that off.
